# A pattern whose DFA doubles with every repeat ("an 'a' 18 bytes before the
# 'c'") is stopped during subset construction, long before it exhausts
# memory, with the same located error as a DFA over the limit
# error: lexer_dfa_explosion.grammar:10:1:
# error: the lexer DFA is too large
@lexer
tokens
    t, eof, err

[ab]* 'a' [ab]{18} 'c'  → t
.                       → err

@parser
top! = ERR → 1
